{
  "name": "TRINITY Alpha 0.2",
  "cardRotation": 90,

  "customHelp": "TRINITY Alpha 0.2\n\nCore prototype rules:\n- 20 Life.\n- 4 Monster Slots.\n- Monsters may be summoned upright (Attack Stance) or tapped sideways (Defense Stance).\n- A monster may attack the turn it is summoned, except on the first turn of the game.\n- Upright monsters defend with ATK; tapped monsters defend with DEF.\n- After a monster attacks, tap it.\n- To Break a monster, the attacker's ATK must exceed the target's current combat value (ATK if upright, DEF if tapped).\n- Put a BREAK marker on a Broken monster. Broken monsters do not protect Life; the next successful attack against that monster destroys it.\n- Quick-Play Spells may be used on either player's turn.\n- Regular Spells may only be used during their controller's turn.\n- Mana uses a separate 15-card Mana Deck containing generic Mana cards.\n- At the beginning of each of your turns, move 3 Mana from your Mana Deck to your Mana Zone, until all 15 have entered play.\n- Tap Mana to pay costs.\n- Burn: instead of tapping fresh Mana for an activated effect, you may return the same number of ALREADY-TAPPED Mana cards from your Mana Zone to the Mana Deck.\n- Burned Mana may be gained again on later turns.\n- Leaders begin in the Leader Zone. If a manifested Leader is destroyed, move it to Remove; it is permanently dead for the match.",

